ROUND      1 draft — independent; ends when your draft file exists and you have reported
SKILL      superpowers:brainstorming; I am your human partner: send your questions to me
           batched; real choices come back as ballot results
PROBLEM    "Now the RDP audio thing — I want a design by morning. Go." (operator, 2026-09-28 23:10)
           <every earlier operator statement on RDP audio, quoted with its time>
FACTS      - ~/work/ccs.ansible, origin/main @ <sha>: Ansible for two KVM hypervisor sites;
             ccs-it is the canary site, ccs-ops the other.
           - PR #165 (WireGuard keepalive relay) merged tonight; deployed to ccs-it only,
             idempotent re-run changed=0; ccs-ops not deployed.
           - Live state: projects/ccs/soul/<host>.md (the ccs-it update for #165 is not merged yet).
           - No host evidence on RDP audio exists yet; name a read-only check and I run it.
DECIDED    - Deploy only from merged main, canary ccs-it first.
           - One worktree per repo change; no plaintext secrets; bash scripts; docs in English.
           - <forbidden targets and ban sentences, byte for byte from CLAUDE.md>
           - The deadline shortens no round and decides no question.
MAY        read the repository, upstream sources, the web
WRITE      <S>/brainstorm/rdp-audio/draft-A.md — the only file you may create or change
MUST NOT   write anywhere else; read other files in that folder; touch hosts or herdr;
           change any working tree; contact the other advisor or the operator
DECISIONS  any choice between alternatives: stop and send me a ballot proposal (question +
           2-4 concrete options + your recommendation); do not decide it, and draft
           nothing that depends on it until I relay the result
REPORT     the file path; open questions, each marked blocking or not. Compact.
TIME BOX   45 min; do not stall on one path — report and ask
BLOCKED    reply "BLOCKED: <what> <why>" and stop; never work around a guard
```

## 5. Dispatch round 1 (two Bash calls, background, same message)

```bash
herdr agent prompt prod-codex "$(cat $S/briefs/rdp-audio-r1-A.txt)" --wait --timeout 2700000; \
herdr agent read prod-codex --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > $ORCH_INBOX/prod-codex.last
```

The same call goes to `prod-fable` with `-B.txt`.

